  "conclusions": [
    "Adding explicit button:left beside existing buttons1 in two CDP held moves is a narrow defensible test-transport correction supported by protocol field distinctions, primary implementation precedent and retained controls.",
    "The CDP control differs from original only by explicit held-left fields, repeated finite32 gestures, diagnostic label and relocated imports/evidence path; whole-source reconstruction confirms its assertions were not weakened.",
    "The native PID/focused sendInputEvent comparison uses a different transport, explicitly focuses the BrowserWindow and integer DIP coordinates. It is supporting comparison, not an identical one-variable experiment.",
    "Both32-gesture controls retained COMPLETE5 and exact45/25/order/drop assertions. These are ROOT execution receipts; reviewer independently read/asserted them, did not execute GUI.",
    "Focus diagnostic reproduces lostpointercapture while document focused/active viewport and no focus-events. Document-blur explanation is not observed there; native OS focus was not independently recorded in that failing run.",
    "The protocol permits optional button; current evidence supports making held state explicit, not claiming original omitted button always invalid or a proven Chromium implementation bug."
  ],
  "limits": [
